    "publisher": "USDA Forest Service, Forest Products Laboratory",
    "where": "Table 5–3b, \"Strength properties of some commercially important woods grown in the United States (inch–pound)\", pp. 5–9 to 5–13: the 12% rows, columns \"Specific gravity\" and \"Static bending, Modulus of elasticity (10^6 lbf in–2)\". Footnote b: \"Specific gravity is based on weight when ovendry and volume when green or at 12% moisture content.\" Footnote c: \"Modulus of elasticity measured from a simply supported, center-loaded beam, on a span depth ratio of 14/1. To correct for shear deflection, the modulus can be increased by 10%.\" Values are for clear, straight-grained specimens; lumber with knots and cross grain is less stiff.",
